-- title:
--   Rank two freeness of ℚₚ⊗ TₚJ_H(M) over the Hecke algebra
-- statement:
--   Fix natural numbers $M$ and $p$ with $M \neq 0$ and $p$ prime, a subgroup $H \leq (\mathbb{Z}/M)^{\times}$, and a finite set $S$ of natural numbers. Assume [`ModularCurve.HeckeDiamondInputsHAll M H`](def/ModularCurve_XHOperators.html#L113), that is: for every prime $\ell$ the package `HeckeInputsHAlong` holds for $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$, $M$, $H$, $\ell$ (the $\beta$-map is defined, $\alpha$ and $\beta$ are integral over $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$, principal divisors exist for the base change to $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$ of the top function field of level $M\ell$, $\alpha$ is finite along, and the fundamental identity for $\beta$ together with the norm formula for $\alpha$ hold); and for each $d \in (\mathbb{Z}/M)^{\times}$ there is an automorphism $\sigma$ of the base-changed function field `xHFunctionFieldBar M H` over $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$ satisfying `IsDiamondAutHBar M H d σ`, i.e. $\sigma$ acts on ratios of integral $q$-expansions of modular forms of any weight on $\Gamma_H(M)$ by the slash action of any $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M)$ with upper-left entry congruent to $d$ modulo $M$. Let $J_H(M) = \mathrm{Pic}^0$ of `xHFunctionFieldBar M H` over $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$ (degree-zero divisors modulo principal ones), and let $T_p J_H(M)$ be the $p$-adic Tate module, realised as the group of sequences $(x_n)$ in $J_H(M)$ with $p^n x_n = 0$ and $p x_{n+1} = x_n$. For each generator $g$ of the index type [`CohCarrier.Gen M ↑S`](def/CohCarrier_Inst.html#L13) — a prime $\ell \notin S$ with $\ell \nmid M$ giving $T_\ell$, a prime $q \mid M$ giving $U_q$ (both realised by `heckeOperatorHAlong`), or an element $d \in (\mathbb{Z}/M)^{\times}$ giving the diamond operator `diamondHBar`), let `tateGenOpH M H ↑S p g` be the induced $\mathbb{Z}_p$-endomorphism of $T_pJ_H(M)$ and let its base change along $\mathbb{Z}_p \to \mathbb{Q}_p$ act on $\mathbb{Q}_p \otimes_{\mathbb{Z}_p} T_pJ_H(M)$. The conclusion is that $\mathbb{Q}_p \otimes_{\mathbb{Z}_p} T_pJ_H(M)$ admits a basis indexed by `Fin 2` over the $\mathbb{Q}_p$-subalgebra of its endomorphism ring generated by these base-changed operators; equivalently, it is free of rank two over that Hecke–diamond algebra.
--
--   This is the rational Eichler–Shimura freeness statement: away from the excluded finite set $S$ of primes, the rational $p$-adic Tate module of the Jacobian of $X_H(M)$ is free of rank two over the algebra generated by the Hecke operators $T_\ell$, $U_q$ and the diamond operators. It is the input used to produce two-dimensional Galois representations with coefficients in the Hecke algebra, and it is cited in the analysis of the ordinary filtration of $T_pJ_H(M)$ (inertia eigenspaces, the multiplicative submodule and the decomposition characters) and in the computation of the trace and determinant of the Galois action on the associated lattice.
